The last four lines are the reason this layout was NOT adopted. With the arena
on the heap the radios have room -- BLE even comes up with Wi-Fi still running
-- but the arena cannot be taken back afterwards: 265 808 bytes free and the
largest single block is 112 628. Tearing the whole BLE stack down does not
repair it. A node that could listen once and never again is not a node.
